"lines": [
{
"text": "Among the creatures the Lord God formed,",
"start": 11.541,
"end": 15.681
},
{
"text": "none was as sly as the serpent.",
"start": 17.581,
"end": 19.721
},
{
"text": "He turned to the woman:",
"start": 21.901,
"end": 23.841
},
{
"text": "Did God close every garden tree to you?",
"start": 25.541,
"end": 29.082
},
{
"text": "She answered him: We eat the fruit",
"start": 30.982,
"end": 34.142
},
{
"text": "from trees throughout the garden.",
"start": 35.922,
"end": 39.222
},
{
"text": "Only the tree at its center is barred.",
"start": 39.842,
"end": 43.662
},
{
"text": "God told us not to eat its fruit,",
"start": 43.923,
"end": 46.703
},
{
"text": "not even to touch it,",
"start": 47.623,
"end": 52.683
},
{
"text": "lest we die.",
"start": 52.823,
"end": 53.963
},
{
"text": "The serpent replied:",
"start": 57.423,
"end": 59.663
},
{
"text": "No death will come from this.",
"start": 61.103,
"end": 63.604
},
{
"text": "God knows the day you taste it,",
"start": 66.024,
"end": 69.464
},
{
"text": "your eyes will come awake.",
"start": 70.884,
"end": 73.504
},
{
"text": "Like gods you will discern",
"start": 73.984,
"end": 76.644
},
{
"text": "what is good and what is evil.",
"start": 76.844,
"end": 83.205
},
{
"text": "She saw food in its branches,",
"start": 86.665,
"end": 89.045
},
{
"text": "beauty before her eyes,",
"start": 91.125,
"end": 93.485
},
{
"text": "something fair to ponder.",
"start": 95.045,
"end": 97.606
},
{
"text": "She plucked and ate the fruit,",
"start": 98.446,
"end": 100.306
},
{
"text": "passed it to her husband there beside her;",
"start": 100.606,
"end": 103.926
},
{
"text": "he ate as well.",
"start": 105.246,
"end": 106.606
},
{
"text": "Then both could see, and knew",
"start": 107.026,
"end": 109.526
},
{
"text": "their nakedness. They joined",
"start": 110.046,
"end": 111.946
},
{
"text": "the leaves of figs by hand",
"start": 111.986,
"end": 114.467
},
{
"text": "and wrapped themselves.",
"start": 114.527,
"end": 116.167
},
{
"text": "That afternoon they heard His voice,",
"start": 116.207,
"end": 119.467
},
{
"text": "the Lord God walking through the garden.",
"start": 119.807,
"end": 123.327
},
{
"text": "Adam and his wife turned from His face",
"start": 124.947,
"end": 128.087
},
{
"text": "and hid within the trees.",
"start": 129.687,
"end": 132.468
},
{
"text": "He called out to Adam:",
"start": 138.068,
"end": 139.708
},
{
"text": "Adam, where are you now?",
"start": 141.028,
"end": 144.468
},
{
"text": "I heard You walking in the garden;",
"start": 144.848,
"end": 147.568
},
{
"text": "naked, I was afraid,",
"start": 147.748,
"end": 149.749
},
{
"text": "and hid.",
"start": 150.289,
"end": 151.089
},
{
"text": "Who told you you were naked?",
"start": 151.949,
"end": 154.429
},
{
"text": "Did you take and eat",
"start": 154.989,
"end": 156.569
},
{
"text": "from the tree I alone forbade?",
"start": 157.089,
"end": 160.089
},
{
"text": "Adam said: The woman You gave",
"start": 160.389,
"end": 162.749
},
{
"text": "to live beside me handed me",
"start": 162.889,
"end": 165.189
},
{
"text": "its fruit; I ate.",
"start": 165.249,
"end": 166.69
},
{
"text": "To the woman God said:",
"start": 167.05,
"end": 168.99
},
{
"text": "What have you done?",
"start": 169.65,
"end": 171.11
},
{
"text": "The serpent tricked me, she replied;",
"start": 172.49,
"end": 175.09
},
{
"text": "I ate.",
"start": 175.47,
"end": 175.85
},
{
"text": "God said to the serpent:",
"start": 179.13,
"end": 181.59
},
{
"text": "Because of this, the curse falls on you",
"start": 183.33,
"end": 187.491
},
{
"text": "above the herd and every beast of earth.",
"start": 187.751,
"end": 192.511
},
{
"text": "Your breast and belly shall bear you;",
"start": 192.951,
"end": 196.171
},
{
"text": "earth will be your food",
"start": 196.411,
"end": 199.111
},
{
"text": "through all your days.",
"start": 199.231,
"end": 201.032
},
{
"text": "I will make enmity stand",
"start": 202.732,
"end": 204.732
},
{
"text": "between you and the woman,",
"start": 204.792,
"end": 206.092
},
{
"text": "your seed and hers.",
"start": 206.152,
"end": 207.372
},
{
"text": "He will keep watch against your head,",
"start": 207.392,
"end": 209.812
},
{
"text": "and you against his heel.",
"start": 210.552,
"end": 212.212
},
{
"text": "To the woman: Your pain and groaning",
"start": 212.752,
"end": 214.892
},
{
"text": "I will multiply. In pain",
"start": 216.852,
"end": 219.293
},
{
"text": "you will bring children forth.",
"start": 220.573,
"end": 223.073
},
{
"text": "To your husband you will submit;",
"start": 223.253,
"end": 226.493
},
{
"text": "he will hold rule over you.",
"start": 228.053,
"end": 231.293
},
{
"text": "To Adam: You heard your wife",
"start": 231.353,
"end": 233.813
},
{
"text": "and ate from the tree I marked",
"start": 235.173,
"end": 237.014
},
{
"text": "as the one you must not eat.",
"start": 237.194,
"end": 239.154
},
{
"text": "The earth is cursed under your work;",
"start": 240.534,
"end": 243.514
},
{
"text": "with pain you will live from it",
"start": 244.034,
"end": 246.554
},
{
"text": "all your days.",
"start": 247.034,
"end": 248.274
},
{
"text": "It will give you thorn and thistle;",
"start": 249.554,
"end": 251.514
},
{
"text": "the herbs of the field",
"start": 251.934,
"end": 253.995
},
{
"text": "will be your food.",
"start": 254.955,
"end": 256.355
},
{
"text": "Your face will sweat for bread",
"start": 256.755,
"end": 258.655
},
{
"text": "till you go back to the earth",
"start": 259.395,
"end": 262.655
},
{
"text": "from which you came. For you are earth;",
"start": 262.815,
"end": 266.375
},
{
"text": "to earth you will return.",
"start": 266.455,
"end": 270.175
},
{
"text": "Adam gave his wife the name Life,",
"start": 272.496,
"end": 275.856
},
{
"text": "for she was mother of all who live.",
"start": 276.156,
"end": 279.116
},
{
"text": "The Lord God made garments of skin",
"start": 281.056,
"end": 284.716
},
{
"text": "for Adam and his wife",
"start": 285.236,
"end": 287.116
},
{
"text": "and clothed them.",
"start": 288.356,
"end": 289.437
},
{
"text": "Then God said: Adam is now",
"start": 290.717,
"end": 294.217
},
{
"text": "as one of us in knowing",
"start": 296.297,
"end": 298.197
},
{
"text": "good from evil. Lest he reach",
"start": 299.577,
"end": 301.617
},
{
"text": "for the tree of life, eat,",
"start": 303.517,
"end": 306.238
},
{
"text": "and live forever.",
"start": 307.918,
"end": 309.158
},
{
"text": "So the Lord God sent him",
"start": 312.098,
"end": 315.718
},
{
"text": "from the garden of Delight to work",
"start": 317.358,
"end": 320.938
},
{
"text": "the earth from which he came.",
"start": 321.858,
"end": 324.619
},
{
"text": "He drove Adam out and settled him",
"start": 324.679,
"end": 327.859
},
{
"text": "across from Delight's garden.",
"start": 328.019,
"end": 330.639
},
{
"text": "He stationed cherubs there,",
"start": 332.179,
"end": 334.079
},
{
"text": "and the turning sword of fire",
"start": 335.279,
"end": 337.819
},
{
"text": "to keep the path",
"start": 339.079,
"end": 340.159
},
{
"text": "to the tree of life.",
"start": 340.179,
"end": 345.5
}
],
